1.1.0 2026-10-26

- Fork MaxMind-DB-Reader-onlyXS: only the XS functions are left, no wrapper
  modules and no dependency on MaxMind::DB::Reader, Moo and others.
- Loading the module no longer loads Math::Int64, Math::Int128, strict and
  warnings. Math::Int128 is loaded on the first uint128 value.
- A database handle is now a reference with ext magic instead of
  a packed pointer, it can not be stored as a string. Anything else passed as
  a handle (undef, a string) croaks instead of crashing perl, a closed handle
  croaks, closing twice is fine, and the database is closed when the handle is
  freed.
- New __value_for_address( $handle, $ip, @path ): one value of the record
  (MMDB_aget_value), the rest of the record is not decoded: several times
  faster than __data_for_address when only some fields are needed.
- New __lookup_for_address: the same, and returns the prefix length of the
  network of the record too.
- A callback of _iterate_search_tree can not use the database after closing
  or freeing it: _close_mmdb dies while the walk runs and the handle is kept
  alive until it is over (the database was freed under the walk before). The
  arguments of the lookup functions are read before the handle is used, a
  tied argument can not close it under them. The typemap is not needed any
  more and is removed; a failed allocation of the handle is checked.
- A NUL byte in a file name, an address or an element of a path is an error
  instead of cutting the string.
- POD: the description of the new functions and an example.
- Print node numbers and data offsets in error messages as unsigned numbers.
- Add the repository and the bug tracker to the META files (MetaResources).
- Initialise the entry data list pointers before the error paths free them.
- Only 64-bit platforms are supported (a 128-bit integer type is needed, as
  before); the code for perls with 32-bit IVs is removed.
- POD of all functions, LICENSE and the license in dist.ini are the
  Artistic License 2.0 of the upstream distribution, not Perl_5.
- Update c/ppport.h (Devel::PPPort 3.68).
- The version is set in dist.ini (OverridePkgVersion), the maxmind-db
  submodule with the test data is restored.
- New tests: t/lookup.t (ipv4/ipv6/mixed databases with all record sizes, all
  data types, broken databases, errors), t/lazy-load.t, t/usage.t, t/value.t and t/tree.t
  (_iterate_search_tree, __read_node, every function with a bad handle).
  The old tests of MaxMind::DB::Reader are removed.
- dev/: cpm based development dependencies (dev.pl, exec.pl, clean-dev.pl),
  dev/test-libmaxminddb.pl to run the tests against given libmaxminddb
  versions (checked with 1.9.1 and 1.14.1) and dev/bench.pl, which compares the
  startup and lookup cost with MaxMind::DB::Reader and
  MaxMind::DB::Reader::XS (replaces tools/).
- Remove .mailmap and CONTRIBUTING.md, rewrite README.md.

1.000009 2022-04-11

- Release with updated ppport.h. No other changes.

1.000008 2019-06-18

- Add deprecation notice

1.000007 2018-12-15

- Explicitly depend on Math::Int64 and Math::Int128. Reported by
  pkdetlefsen. GitHub #27.


1.000006 2018-10-16

- The performance of record_for_address has been improved.
- Strings retuned by record_for_address will now always have the
  utf8 flag on. Previously, the flag would not be set if the string
  was all ASCII.


1.000005 2018-04-12

- Fixed tests to work with recent `libmaxminddb` releases. PR by
  Hidenori Sugiyama. GitHub #22.


1.000004 2017-01-25

- Command line arguments to Build.PL are now passed through, allowing building
  with option install_base. PR by Mickey. GitHub #18.


1.000003 2016-03-23

- iterate_search_tree() now works with libmaxminddb 1.2.0+. GitHub #12.


1.000002 2016-01-07

- Fixed test failures with the latest version of libmaxminddb (1.1.3).


1.000001 2015-12-21

- Fixed test failures with the latest version of libmaxminddb (1.1.2).


1.000000 2014-09-22

- First production release.


0.070000 2014-09-15

- An exception is no longer thrown when a private IP address is passed to
  record_for_address. Instead a lookup will be done in the database, and
  undef will be returned if there is no record for the IP.


0.060004 2014-04-21

- Updated to latest tests from pure Perl reader. Fixes GH #3.


0.060003 2014-03-10

- Added basic docs for this distro.


0.060002 2013-12-30

- Error messages should now be the same for the pure Perl and XS readers.

- Added some more tests and made a small internals change to faciliate said
  tests.


0.060001 2013-12-17

- First public release. We've been using this at MaxMind, Inc. for a while and
  it seems to be stable. Bug reports to the contrary are welcome.
